# .dockerignore — keep the Docker build context small.
#
# Every entry here is a file/dir that the Dockerfile does NOT need.
# Smaller context = faster build, fewer chances to leak secrets, and a
# tighter image. The runtime image is built FROM the builder stage
# artifacts (`/opt/venv`, `data/index.sqlite`); this file is about what
# we send over the wire INTO the builder.

# VCS, CI, and project metadata that bloat the context.
.git
.gitignore
.github

# Local-only state (skill registry, OpenMemory cache, SDD artifacts).
.atl
.engram
openspec

# Virtualenv + Python cache.
.venv
__pycache__
*.py[cod]

# Linter / test caches.
.ruff_cache
.pytest_cache
test-results
playwright-report

# Local dev fixtures and the pre-baked vector index (the builder
# produces a fresh one with `python -m mcp_server.interfaces.cli.preindex`).
data/index.sqlite
data/index.sqlite-*

# Docker compose variants not used by the deploy workflow.
docker-compose*.yml

# Markdown docs — README is whitelisted because pyproject.toml points
# at it (`readme = "README.md"`). The Dockerfile COPY chains it back in.
*.md
!README.md
